    @* Deploy SQLWATCH / Deploy Darling Perf Monitor cards removed 2026-07-21 —
       see RouteConstants.cs "Deployment" for why. Do not re-add. *@
    <div class="guide-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-server"></i> Monitoring New Server</h2>
        <p>
            Add a SQL Server instance under <strong>Servers</strong> and SQLTriage connects to it directly —
            no agent and no collector database are required. SQLTriage's checks run against the instance's
            own DMVs.
        </p>
        <p>
            If a SQLWATCH or PerformanceMonitor database already exists on the instance, SQLTriage will
            <strong>read</strong> it and light up the matching dashboards. SQLTriage does not install,
            deploy, or upgrade either one — installing a third-party collector is a change your DBA makes
            deliberately, under your own change control.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-section">
